# REQUIRES: python-api, torch
# Read-only DLPack views of a simulation on the CPU (D[python-dlpack]),
# scenario torch of Inputs/python_dlpack.py: PyTorch as the consumer. The
# feature `torch` is set when the interpreter of the tests imports torch,
# or when lit is given -Dtorch_python=<an interpreter with torch>.
# RUN: %torch_python %S/Inputs/python_dlpack.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU torch | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: Double: torch shares the buffers (float64, float64) on the CPU; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: Mixed: torch shares the buffers (float64, float64) on the CPU; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: Mixed, not deterministic: torch shares the buffers (float64, float32) on the CPU; aliases hold their leases
# CHECK: a tensor outlives its simulation; its blocks go to no other simulation while it lives
# CHECK: dlpack torch passed
